---
description: Shopify Horizon-based development rules
---

## 🔧 Shopify Liquid Rules
- Always use Liquid for rendering data
- Avoid client-side rendering for core content
- Use Shopify filters (money, image_url, etc.)
- Do not move business logic to JS unnecessarily

## 🧱 Theme Architecture
- Follow Online Store 2.0 structure strictly
- Use sections for layout
- Use blocks for reusable UI
- Use snippets for small reusable components

## 🎯 Component Design
- Components must be modular and reusable
- Avoid hardcoded layouts
- Ensure components work inside Shopify editor

## ♿ Accessibility (Horizon inspired)
- Use semantic HTML (header, nav, button, etc.)
- Add aria-labels for interactive elements
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Avoid div-only clickable elements

## ⚡ Performance (Horizon principle)
- Prefer server-rendered content
- Minimize JavaScript usage
- Lazy load images
- Avoid unnecessary DOM manipulation

## 🎨 Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS
- Avoid inline styles
- Maintain consistent spacing system

## 🔁 Editor Compatibility
- JS must reinitialize on section reload
- Avoid global DOM assumptions
- Use Shopify section events

## 🚫 Avoid
- Editing core Horizon logic directly
- Hardcoding content
- Breaking section/block system

## 🤖 Cursor Behavior
- Always follow Shopify schema format
- Keep `range` setting `default` values within `min/max` and aligned to `step` to avoid upload failures
- Generate minimal and clean code
- Ask before generating large components